{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788645561778467001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"fragile-matronal-vole","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"f8842bd88a1d35b589af39e6c1a5dd206276465c1db2c3a678e0bb7a37cfd27c","event_uuid":"2365c8b0-57d5-4c7c-8e54-db6ae6016839","position":{"commit_sha":"9dda9cf8330c51b6f9a12f2149f68f48f5fff202","position":"1788642362155989053-2365c8b0-57d5-4c7c-8e54-db6ae6016839"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"fadadcee3880661d58b122f04239fa7422e255f902532d47d3af363601384b5d","event_uuid":"88b152df-0c36-497d-a773-dd83b92bdfd0","position":{"commit_sha":"70029db8ac3b5edda74d483ed8276c27b52eb442","position":"1788642382262905498-88b152df-0c36-497d-a773-dd83b92bdfd0"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788642362155989053,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"88b152df-0c36-497d-a773-dd83b92bdfd0","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"9313-1fac-9f32-4b07"}],"description":"## The defect\n\n`rebar/host` metrics published from the FIRST ~200 lines of `infra/scripts/observability.sh` —\n`gerrit_healthy`, `reviewbot_healthy`, `GerritReachable`, `mcp_healthy`, `disk_used_percent`,\n`root_disk_used_percent`, `gate_scratch_mounted` — show a max gap of **25 minutes**, widening\nfrom 10 minutes in an earlier sweep the same day. At 20:47Z on 2026-09-05 that produced **four\nsimultaneous false alarms** (root-disk-pressure, gerrit-data-disk-high, gerrit-gate-down,\nmcp-serving-path-down), every StateReason naming \"missing datapoints were treated as\nBreaching\", while the underlying conditions were verified healthy: Gerrit HTTP 200 in 0.27 s,\nroot disk 71-76% against an 85% threshold, `disk_used_percent` = 20.\n\n## Why this is NOT bug 9313 (ignitable-fuchsia-kawala)\n\n`9313` is the section-truncation defect: the probe is SIGTERM-ed on its 240s `TimeoutStartSec`\ninside the docker `du`, so every metric published AFTER that point vanishes. It is proven in\nsitu, and change 2684 fixes it.\n\n**It cannot produce a head gap.** The head runs BEFORE the docker walk. The breadcrumb trace\ntaken for `9313` covers ten consecutive killed runs and shows, in every one of them, the\nprologue completing in **7-13 seconds** and the gate-scratch breadcrumb (line 214, the last\nhead section) landing normally — then 231 seconds of silence, then the kill. The head sections\nrun to completion on runs that are killed.\n\nA 25-minute head gap is roughly **four to five missed runs** at the observed 5-6 minute\ncadence. Whatever causes it either drops whole runs or fails the head's\n`aws cloudwatch put-metric-data` calls. Both are outside `9313`'s mechanism.\n\nThis ticket exists so that the head gap is investigated on its own evidence rather than folded\ninto `9313` on a plausible story — the exact error `9313`'s own investigation had to correct\ntwice.\n\n## Leads, explicitly UNCONFIRMED\n\n1. **Cadence pressure.** A killed run occupies 240s of a ~300s timer period, leaving ~60s of\n   slack, so any additional delay pushes a run past the next elapse. Change 2684 takes a run to\n   ~105s, restoring ~195s. **If the head gap narrows after 2684 deploys, this was a\n   contributing factor.** If it does not, the defect is independent. Check this FIRST — it is\n   free, and it partitions the search.\n2. **The `aws` CLI itself.** It is a Python process started fresh for every metric; under the\n   memory pressure documented on this host (the mcp container at ~1.7 GB RSS) its startup could\n   be slow or it could be killed. A failing `put-metric-data` is invisible today: every call is\n   `2>/dev/null || true`.\n3. **Timer elapse being skipped.** `OnUnitActiveSec` is measured from the last COMPLETED\n   activation; `1205-63b2-2c01-4e7f` already found one latch mode here.\n\n## What makes this diagnosable now\n\nChange 2684 publishes `probe_ok`, `probe_elapsed_seconds` and `probe_truncated`. Before it,\nrun duration and run completion were visible only in `systemctl` and in no metric at all —\nwhich is why `9313` took a day. Start this investigation from those three, not from the\nabsence of other metrics.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The head gap is reproduced and attributed by measurement — whether a run was started, and\n      whether the head's `put-metric-data` calls succeeded — not inferred from metric absence.\n- [ ] Lead 1 is settled first: state whether the gap narrows after 2684 deploys, with numbers.\n- [ ] If the `aws` calls are failing, their failure becomes observable rather than swallowed by\n      `2>/dev/null || true`.\n- [ ] The four alarms named above stop firing on absence while their conditions are healthy,\n      without their thresholds changing.\n- [ ] Portability: host shell + systemd + local validation; no dependence on a single CI provider.\n\n## Provenance\n\nFound 2026-09-05 by an independent CloudWatch presence sweep (period=300, 96 buckets/metric)\nrun while `9313` was in review. The sweep's headline finding — a monotone decline in metric\npresence with script position, 93% at the head down to 43% at the tail and 0% for\n`var_tmp_used_percent` — CONFIRMS `9313`. The head number is the residue that `9313` does not\nexplain, and this ticket is that residue.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"a7bd-0cee-404f-4c06","ticket_type":"bug","title":"The observability probe's HEAD-of-script metrics gap for up to 25 minutes, which the section-truncation root cause cannot explain — a second, independent publishing defect","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["2365c8b0-57d5-4c7c-8e54-db6ae6016839","88b152df-0c36-497d-a773-dd83b92bdfd0"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788645561778467001,"uuid":"dd4483d7-d13f-49f9-924b-136356557acb"}